+# Arcium SettingsUI vendor snapshot
+
+This snapshot is copied from committed package revisions for offline SwiftPM builds.
+
+- SettingsUI: local `SettingsUI` checkout, revision `164b8920aa7fd388d560d3e7e706f65e477d21ff`.
+- ColorTokensKit-Swift: revision `cba1f4c857412f9f241efce4ce79302c487710f2`, package version `0.3.0`.
+- SettingsUI manifest delta: replace the exact remote ColorTokensKit dependency with `.package(path: "../ColorTokensKit-Swift")`. No other upstream manifest field is changed.
+- SettingsUI has no tracked LICENSE file at the source revision; its README is retained. ColorTokensKit's `MIT-LICENSE.txt` is retained.
+- No `.git`, `.build`, tests, examples, or package resolution cache is included. ColorTokensKit's `Resources/ColorPalettes.json` is retained because its target declares it as a processed resource.
+- The host package owns the dynamic `ArciumSettingsUI` product and any host preset resources.
+
+Trailing whitespace in vendored text files is normalized for Chromium patch checks.
+
+ColorTokensKit resource loading is adapted to resolve its bundle from the signed
+application Resources directory, without a developer build-path fallback in apps.
+Standalone SwiftPM test processes retain the generated module bundle lookup.
+
+SettingsColumnResizeHandle keeps keyboard and accessibility resizing, with a
+small themed focus marker replacing macOS's full-height focus outline.
+
+Shared palette and color-adjustment components are adopted from SettingsUI
+revision `5cfbc34` on `feature/public-palette-controls`. Only the two additive
+public component files are ported; existing host adaptations remain.
